Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Cosmological Correlators", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"53bc1315-6804-4a2d-8be7-1a2994805da3"],

Cell["\<\
The command CosmoTreeMB constructs the MB representation of the time integral \
of a tree graph, T(x, y) = Integrate[Product[t_v^(r_v - 1) Exp[-x_v t_v], v] \
Product[BesselK[\[Nu]_l, y_l t_l^>] BesselI[\[Nu]_l, y_l t_l^<], l]], as one \
balanced MB integral for every orientation of its lines (Section 6.4 of the \
paper). The integral is the sum over the orientations of the prefactors times \
the values of these MB integrals.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c4429693-9317-4a22-8860-1f0fb1a2682f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Two-Site Chain in Power-Law FRW Cosmology", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"07e7753a-83b9-4b53-8de4-31e2be99d218"],

Cell["\<\
Conformally coupled scalars with cubic interactions in a power-law FRW \
cosmology, a(\[Eta]) ~ (-\[Eta])^(-1 - \[Epsilon]). Every orientation gives a \
two-fold MB integral; the option \"Point\" specifies a kinematic point at \
which its variables lie in the unit interval.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3b616839-26c5-4644-a782-283ea99e7050"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"T2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CosmoTreeMB", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "\[Epsilon]"}], ",", " ", 
